  "bodyText": "New Session\nPlugins\nAutomation tasks\nMore\nWorkspaces\nNo sessions yet\nMore\nInto the Unknown\nPreview\nChoose workspace\nChoose a workspace to start\nVision Router is ready 🎉\n\nFor first use, remember one thing: the chat model answers, and the vision model reads images. Follow these 3 steps.\n\n1 · Choose your chat model and enable Vision\n\nChoose the model you normally use from the lower-right chat selector. When you need image understanding, click “Vision” immediately to the left of the model selector; the chip lights up in its selected state to mean it is on. Turn it off again when you no longer need it.\n\n2 · Choose the vision model\n\nOpen Settings → Vision Router and choose it under “Vision model”. It only reads images and does not replace your chat model.\n\n3 · Add fallback models\n\nAdd more than one vision model if you want. If one fails, Vision Router tries the next; the built-in free fallback remains available at the end.\n\n×\nLater\nGuide me through vision setup",
